  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The velocity vector $v=\u27e8u,v\u27e9$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=\u27e8{e}^{3t},\\,{t}^{3}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=\u27e8${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83{e}^{3t},\\,3{t}^{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
